+/// X2 T1: does heimdall-proto's parent see heimdall-proto's stops as a job-control shell
+/// does, so that a child stop must be mirrored for the job to look stopped (S2-S5)?
+///
+/// * The parent must be in another process group. A job-control shell puts every job in
+///   a group of its own; a non-job-control script (`sh -c '...; run ...; echo'`) shares
+///   heimdall-proto's group, never sees a stop of its own child, and under plain exec
+///   would not see the stop either. Mirroring there would leave heimdall-proto stopped
+///   with nobody to continue it when the child is continued by PID.
+/// * heimdall-proto must be attached to its session's controlling terminal: one of
+///   stdin/stdout/stderr is that terminal, or (stdio redirected) the terminal's
